  "scope": "The three independent derivations establish the bielliptic, elliptic-Hopf and secondary-Kodaira exclusions for the explicit smooth connected total-space domain. FD compares the independently derived invariant-cycle argument with the retained positive Kaehler-pairing proof; its base reduction and normalization have exact graph and fibre maps. FE compares resonant anticanonical monomials with the retained divisor/full-fibre calculation and finite invariant-ring descent. FF compares the intrinsic effective-line character with the retained primary Picard quotient and norm argument, preserving all six equations and finite factors. The three conclusions and all displayed mathematics are preserved. Postrelease domain/local-family clarifications add no independent credit. C3.1, C3.11, C3.10 and integral-CDP receivers retain their established smooth scope. The F0 receiving paragraph uses the unchanged Hopf contraction/finite-quotient surface description; root exposure there gives no independent F0 credit. No historical program is identified in the17 inspected rows and none is claimed rerun.",
